# Backend

- PHP 8.4 / Laravel 12. Prefer facades and helpers (`request()`, `auth()`) over constructor DI unless the surrounding file already injects.
- Reference classes with `User::class`, never `'App\\Models\\User'`.
- Explicit parameter and return types. Constructor property promotion. `casts(): array` on models.
- Create files with `ddev artisan make:... --no-interaction`. Do not add dependencies without approval.
- Tests are PHPUnit feature tests (`ddev artisan make:test --phpunit`). Do not add Pest tests. Run `ddev artisan test --compact` on the changed file.
- Before migrations or models, inspect schema with Boost `database-schema`. Before Laravel API changes, use `search-docs`.

```php
// ❌ BAD
public function store()
{
    $user = User::where('email', request('email'))->first();
}

// ✅ GOOD
public function store(): RedirectResponse
{
    $user = User::query()->where('email', request('email'))->first();

    return redirect()->route('dashboard');
}
```
